## Workflow overview

harness-maker provides 4 stages; `$hm-research` is optional.
Invoke a stage by mentioning the skill name (e.g. `$hm-execute task-slug`).
Use this Codex spelling in next-step and recovery guidance; recommend only available skills.

### Stages

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `$hm-research` | Optional: facts, prior art, alternatives; writes RESEARCH doc |
| `$hm-spec` | Acceptance criteria, irreversible decisions; writes SPEC doc |
| `$hm-execute` | PLAN, tests RED, code GREEN, one review; no commits |
| `$hm-wrapup` | `hm check`, memory, single commit |

Each stage stops when it is done; the next one is the user's call, or the world model's under its Advance rule.

